Sure. For your Quiz App → Minikube deployment, the main steps are:

Build the Docker images
Build the backend and frontend images.
Load the Docker images of backend and frontend into Minikube
Make the images available inside your quiz-app Minikube cluster.
Create Kubernetes Secrets
Store the backend .env values securely, especially the MongoDB connection.
Create the Backend Deployment
Run the backend container as a Kubernetes Pod.
Create the Backend Service
Give the backend a Kubernetes network endpoint that the frontend can reach.
Test the Backend
Confirm the backend Pod and Service are working.
Create the Frontend Deployment
Run the frontend container as a Kubernetes Pod.
Create the Frontend Service
Expose the frontend so you can access the application from your browser.
Configure Frontend → Backend communication
Make sure the browser can reach the Kubernetes backend Service.
Access and test the Quiz App
Open the frontend in your browser and test the complete application.



